==============================
FLYWAY MIGRATION CHEAT SHEET
==============================

1. Maven Dependency (pom.xml)

<dependency>
    <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
    <artifactId>flyway-core</artifactId>
</dependency>

<dependency>
    <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
    <artifactId>flyway-database-postgresql</artifactId>
</dependency>


------------------------------------

2. application.properties

spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/BankDB
spring.datasource.username=postgres
spring.datasource.password=your_password

spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=validate

spring.flyway.enabled=true
spring.flyway.locations=classpath:db/migrations
spring.flyway.baseline-on-migrate=true

------------------------------------

3. Folder Structure

src
└── main
    └── resources
        └── db
            └── migrations
                V1__create_table.sql
                V2__add_column.sql
                V3__rename_column.sql

------------------------------------

4. Migration Naming

✅ Correct

V1__create_table.sql
V2__add_column.sql
V3__rename_column.sql

❌ Wrong

V1_create_table.sql
version1.sql
migration.sql

------------------------------------

5. Migration Order

V1
↓
V2
↓
V3
↓
V4

Each version must be unique.

------------------------------------

6. Common SQL

Create Table

CREATE TABLE customer(
    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100)
);

Add Column

ALTER TABLE customer
ADD COLUMN email VARCHAR(100);

Rename Column

ALTER TABLE customer
RENAME COLUMN email TO customer_email;

Change Data Type

ALTER TABLE customer
ALTER COLUMN age TYPE INTEGER;

Set NOT NULL

ALTER TABLE customer
ALTER COLUMN age SET NOT NULL;

Drop NOT NULL

ALTER TABLE customer
ALTER COLUMN age DROP NOT NULL;

------------------------------------

7. Common Mistakes

❌ Wrong

ALTER COLUMN age integer;

✅ Correct

ALTER COLUMN age TYPE integer;

------------------------------------

8. Duplicate Version

❌ Wrong

V2__change.sql
V2__rename.sql

✅ Correct

V2__change.sql
V3__rename.sql

------------------------------------

9. Flyway History Table

flyway_schema_history

Stores:
- Version
- Description
- Checksum
- Status

------------------------------------

10. Best Practices

✔ Commit migration files to GitHub.
✔ Never edit an executed migration.
✔ Create a new migration for every schema change.
✔ Test migrations locally.
✔ Keep version numbers sequential.

------------------------------------

11. Git Commands

git add .
git commit -m "Add Flyway migration"
git push origin main

------------------------------------

12. Remember

• Use V1, V2, V3...
• Double underscore (__) is required.
• One version = One migration.
• Flyway runs only pending migrations.
• SQL error stops application startup.
• Migration files SHOULD be committed to GitHub.